            <ArticleTitle>[Congenital valvular heart disease with high familial penetrance].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>581-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1701/1206.13361</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bicuspid valve aortic (BVA) is one of the most common congenital malformations. Only 20% of patients preserves a normal valve function throughout life. There are sporadic and familial forms, the latter to autosomal dominant. We present a case of familiarity of BVA high penetrance. Patient with aortic stenosis by BVA, is the father of two children with BVA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
